  "interpretation": {
    "limits": "One time step on a 120-cell periodic uniform-velocity contact verifies this normalization interpretation and the audit observer's passivity only. It does not validate apparatus pressure cycles, discharge flow, or general pressure-solver behavior on nonuniform full-apparatus fields.",
    "normalization_factor_limitation": "The v2512 source confirms the GAMG normalized residual divides sum-magnitude residual by normFactor, but the current GAMG log level does not emit normFactor. Ratios computed from the audit's absolute operator L1 residual are a rough estimate only; cancellation at machine precision produces pass-to-pass spread. No solver/source, tolerance or maxIter changes were made.",
    "raw_residual_caveat": "The diagnostic's raw fvMatrix::residual L1 is about 14.82 m3/s because the periodic coupled neighbour source is counted twice in this raw path; the audit identifies an extra coupled-source L1 of the same magnitude. The corrected direct operator residual is the appropriate algebraic defect here.",
    "statement": "All 16 GAMG solves hit 1000 iterations and retained normalized final residuals of roughly 0.067-0.453, so the configured normalized tolerance was not attained. However, the corrected integrated operator defects for the assembled full pressure equation remained at roundoff scale (max per-cell O(1e-16) m3/s; unweighted L1 O(1e-15) m3/s), while p stayed uniform within about 5e-9 Pa. This is consistent with normalization of a nearly-zero periodic pressure system, not a materially unsolved pressure field in this one-step contact case."
  },
